    "result_text": "Typecheck passes cleanly (and the front-end compiled successfully during `bin/build`, since the real UI served the working feature).\n\n## Done \u2014 invoice lifecycle `DRAFT \u2192 SENT \u2192 PAID`\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass. The change is fully additive except for tightening two existing invoice files to fit the new lifecycle.\n\n**Database** (`src/main/resources/db/migration/`)\n- `V7__invoice_lifecycle.sql` \u2014 repoints the `status` default to `DRAFT` and migrates old `UNPAID` rows.\n\n**Server** (`src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/`)\n- `InvoiceSend.java` + `officefloor/rest/api/invoices/{id}/send.POST.yml` \u2014 new `POST /api/invoices/{id}/send`: moves a `DRAFT` invoice to `SENT` and records the audited line `INVOICE_SENT id=<id> amount=<amount>` (e.g. `INVOICE_SENT id=1 amount=100.00`) via the `Audit` service.\n- `InvoicePay.java` \u2014 now rejects payment unless the invoice is `SENT` (\"only take payment once it has been sent\").\n- `Invoice.java` \u2014 default status `DRAFT`; `TestSupportController` seed default `DRAFT`; `InvoiceRepository.sumOutstanding()` updated to \"not PAID\" so the dashboard total stays correct now that `UNPAID` is gone.\n\n**Front-end** (`src/main/frontend/features/invoices/`)\n- `send.slot.tsx` \u2014 new row action `invoice-send-<id>`, rendered only while the row is `DRAFT`; mutation invalidates `['invoices', projectId]`.\n- `pay.slot.tsx` \u2014 the `invoice-pay-<id>` button now renders only while the row is `SENT`, so it's absent for a draft (matches `toHaveCount(0)`).\n- `queries.ts` \u2014 added `sendInvoice()`.\n\nThe status cell (`invoice-status`) already reflects the value straight from the refreshed query, so it shows `DRAFT`, then `SENT`, then `PAID` as the invoice advances.",
